  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`, and the full suite passes (1907 passed).\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py:392`), a child context inherited the parent's whole `default_map`. So a map like `{\"foo\": {\"name\": \"x\"}}` was searched for `name` at the top level and never matched.\n\n**Fix:** the child now takes only its own entry, `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`.\n\nI didn't update `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`, since `CHANGES.md` wasn't checked and the docs didn't seem to need a change. Say if you want a changelog entry.",
